### 1. Get all employees
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees

### 2. Create employee (success -> 201)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nikhil",
  "email": "nikhil@company.com",
  "department": "Engineering"
}

### 3. Create employee (validation error -> 400)  
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "department": ""
}

### 4. Get employee that does not exist (-> 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees/999

### 5. Apply leave (change dates to future dates!)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-03",
  "reason": "Family function"
}

### 6. Apply leave with too many days (-> 400 Insufficient leave balance)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leaves
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-31",
  "reason": "Long vacation"
}

### 7. List all leaves
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves

### 8. List leaves of one employee
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leaves?employeeId=1

### 9. Approve leave 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/leaves/1/approve

### 10. Approve leave 1 AGAIN (-> 400 Only PENDING leave can be updated)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/leaves/1/approve

### 11. Reject a leave
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/leaves/2/reject
